Herdr is a terminal workspace manager for AI coding agents: the agent
terminals (Claude Code, Codex, opencode, Cursor, Grok and others) live
inside a background server, so they keep working when you close the
terminal or drop the network. Sessions and layout are restored after a
restart, panes are marked working/blocked/idle, and additional machines
can be attached over SSH.

Native OpenBSD source build of github.com/herdrdev/herdr (Rust only,
no bundled C libraries). State lives under ~/.local/share/herdr/ and
~/.config/herdr/. The agent CLIs it runs are separate packages or
installs; herdr does not bundle them.
